    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-078 — Media-scoped and multi-selector custom property extraction.** Moves var extraction from the inline top-level parse loop to a post-pass over `result.rules`. Covers two cases ADR-026 deferred.\n\n## The two gaps fixed\n\n**Gap 1 — Multi-selector rules containing `:root` were skipped.**\n```css\n:root, .skin-invert, .notheme { --color-base: #202122 }\n```\nADR-026's extractor required *exactly one* selector that was *exactly* `:root`. This multi-selector pattern (very common in Wikipedia's Vector 2022) was dropped → refs like `color: var(--color-base)` failed silently.\n\n**Gap 2 — `@media`-scoped `:root` rules were skipped.**\n```css\n@media screen { :root { --color-base: #202122 } }\n```\n`parse_media_block()` pushed rules into `result.rules` but never ran the extractor → variables defined inside `@media` blocks never reached `result.variables`.\n\n## What the fix does\n\nPost-pass over `result.rules`:\n- Detects rules containing `:root` in any selector position\n- Skips width-constrained `@media` (parse doesn't know viewport — deferred to cascade-time)\n- Uses ADR-077 `q_*` feature flags for feature-constrained `@media` (skips dark mode, includes light mode)\n- Extracts `--x: val` declarations from matching rules\n\nAlso adds `--*` custom properties to `is_inherited` per CSS Variables spec.\n\n## Verified impact on Wikipedia\n\n| | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Total `var()` uses | 569 | 569 |\n| With fallback (work-around) | 523 | 523 |\n| **Without fallback (fail silently)** | **46** | **~5** |\n\n**5 of 6 previously-failing custom properties now resolve:**\n- `--color-base` — main text color\n- `--color-visited` — visited link color\n- `--color-destructive` — error/danger styling\n- `--border-color-interactive` — interactive borders\n- `--font-size-medium` — medium font size (headings)\n\nVisual difference: link colors, borders, font sizes should be visibly closer to Firefox.\n\n## What this does NOT fix\n\n- **`@media (min-width: ...) { :root { --x } }`** — width-dependent vars remain deferred (needs cascade-time resolution, separate ADR).\n- **Wikipedia's History position** — mobile menu anomaly is `:where()`/`:has()` (076-D), History 1400px offset is ADR-074 Bug B (line-wrap).\n\n## Test changes\n\n- **New:** 5 tests covering each extraction case (multi-selector, `@media screen`, width-constrained skip, dark-mode skip, light-mode include)\n- **Updated:** ADR-026 test \"multi-selector :root rule NOT extracted\" → now \"IS extracted\" (was documenting the old limitation, which is what ADR-078 removes)\n- **Adjacent tests still pass:** `html { --x }`, `.foo { --y }`, `html:root { --z }` — compound selectors correctly skipped\n\n## Test count\n\n702 → 707 cases, 2661 → 2670 assertions. All green.\n\n## Verification category\n\n**Unit-tested (5 new + 1 updated).** Visual verification: manual inspection of Wikipedia link colors, borders, font sizes vs pre-ADR-078.\n\nRefs #285\n",
